  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "the drum and bass two-step: kick on one and on the and of three, snare on two and four, ghosted snares between, a rolling sub under it",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars. The kick answers itself across the bar line (one, the and of three; one, the and of three and its a), the snare is the backbeat at full weight with ghosts a sixteenth before and after, the eighth hats lean on the offbeat and a quiet sixteenth shaker fills the rest. The sub rolls on the root with a step below and a third above, inside a fifth so it fits every key the bass register holds."
  }
